{% block prose %}
<div class="callout">
  <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> a proper tradie website in New Zealand costs roughly <strong>NZ$2,000–$4,000</strong> in 2026 if copywriting and local SEO are included. Under about NZ$1,500 you are usually buying design only. WFT is {{ site.priceDisplay }} flat with everything included, which sits at the bottom of that range because we only build for one industry.</p>
</div>

<h2>Why nobody will tell you the price</h2>
<p>Ring five New Zealand web agencies and four will say "it depends" and try to book a discovery call. Some of that is genuine — scope really does vary. Most of it is that publishing a price invites comparison, and an agency whose main advantage is that you haven't compared them would rather you didn't.</p>
<p>It also makes the whole market harder to judge. If you've never bought a website, a $600 quote and a $6,000 quote look like the same product at different prices. They almost never are.</p>

