<h2>The one question that explains most of the price gap</h2>
<p><strong>"Is the copywriting included?"</strong></p>
<p>Writing a five-page trade website properly — interviewing you, working out what your customers search for, writing headlines and service pages that convert — is typically 10 to 15 hours of skilled work. New Zealand agencies commonly charge NZ$800–$1,500 for it as a standalone service.</p>
<p>When a quote comes in at NZ$800 for a whole website, that work isn't in there. It's been quietly handed back to you. And most tradies who accept that quote never write the copy, so the site either launches with placeholder text or never launches at all.</p>
<p>Ask the question directly and a confusing set of quotes usually resolves itself.</p>

<h2>The costs that don't show up in the quote</h2>

<div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Cost</th><th>Typical NZ price</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>.nz domain renewal</td><td>NZ$30–$50/yr</td><td>Make sure it's registered in <em>your</em> name, not the agency's.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Hosting</td><td>NZ$120–$400/yr</td><td>Cheap hosting is slow hosting, and speed affects ranking.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>SSL certificate</td><td>Usually free</td><td>If someone charges you separately for this, ask why.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Content changes</td><td>NZ$80–$150/hr</td><td>Or included in a managed plan. Worth knowing before you need it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ongoing local SEO</td><td>NZ$150–$400/mo</td><td>Optional, but a site nobody maintains slides down the rankings.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p>The one that catches people is the domain. If your web person registers it in their own name, leaving costs you either a fight or a fee. Always check whose name is on it.</p>

<h2>Three quotes, same brief, different products</h2>
<p>Here's what a tradie in Hamilton typically ends up comparing:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>NZ$750</strong> — five pages, "you supply text and images", 3–4 weeks. Real cost once you value your own writing time: considerably more, and it may never go live.</li>
  <li><strong>NZ$3,200</strong> — five pages, copy included, SEO "available as an add-on" at NZ$600, 4–6 weeks. Real cost: NZ$3,800.</li>
  <li><strong>NZ$6,500</strong> — full brand and site, 8 weeks, everything included. Genuinely good work, and more than most trade businesses need.</li>
</ul>
<p>None of those is a rip-off. They're different products. The mistake is comparing the numbers instead of the scope.</p>

